CORE
real_variable1.sv
--bound 3
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.r == 1\.5 \|\| main\.r == 2\.5: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.r >= 1\.5: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.p2\] always main\.s == 0\.25: PROVED up to bound 3$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Properties over variables of the real types. Counterexample traces of
real variables, the netlist-based engines and conditional assignments to
real variables are not covered yet.
